course: dictionary
lesson: 14618
title: Porcupines and their quills
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Porcupines is the plural of porcupine, which means more than one. One porcupine, two porcupines: you add an s, just like cat and cats.
explain: «The porcupines climbed the tree to eat the bark.» The s on the end tells you there is more than one animal climbing. A porcupine is a large rodent covered in long, sharp quills.
explain: «A family of porcupines slept in a hollow log all day.» A family is a group, so several porcupines live together here. Porcupines are mostly active at night, so they rest during the day.
explain: Quills are the porcupine's armour. «The fox backed away from the porcupine's sharp quills.» The quills protect the porcupine from predators, which are animals that hunt it.
fact: «Porcupines» is the plural of porcupine: two or more of these animals.
fact: A porcupine is a large rodent covered in long, sharp quills that protect it from predators.
fact: New World porcupines climb trees in the Americas.
fact: Old World porcupines live on the ground in Africa, Asia and southern Europe.
fact: Porcupines eat plants, bark and fruit, and they are mostly active at night.
exercise: What does «porcupines» mean? | One porcupine | A kind of tree | A sharp needle | *More than one porcupine
exercise: «Porcupines protect themselves with long, sharp quills.» What protects a porcupine? | Its fast running | A thick shell | *Its long, sharp quills | Its loud voice
exercise: What is the plural of porcupine? | porcupiness | porcupinies | *porcupines | porcupine
test: Where do New World porcupines live? | Under the sea | *In trees in the Americas | On the ground in Africa | In southern Europe
test: «The porcupines come out at night to eat bark and fruit.» When are porcupines mostly active? | All the time, without stopping | *At night | In the middle of the day | Only at dawn
exam: Which sentence uses the plural correctly? | Three porcupine waddled through the grass. | Three porcupines is waddling through the grass. | *Three porcupines waddled through the grass. | Three porcupiness waddled through the grass.
